  "heat": 2,
  "text": "Walking in without a summons was a death sentence. She had not been called in thirty days. One law in Persia. Man or woman. You come to the king unsummoned, you die. Unless he holds out the golden sceptre. And Esther tells Mordecai the part that kept her up at night. \"I have not been called to come in unto the king these thirty days.\" Thirty days. She is the queen. And she has no idea where she stands. Mordecai's reply is brutal and kind at once. \"Think not with thyself that thou shalt escape in the king's house, more than all the Jews.\" You are not safe. The palace is not a shelter. Then: if you stay silent, deliverance will arise from another place, but you and your father's house will be destroyed. Hear that. He never says God will fail. He says rescue is coming and you might not be in it. \"And who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for such a time as this?\" A question. Not a command. So she fasts three days and sends back four words: \"If I perish, I perish.\" Third day. Royal apparel. Inner court. And the king holds out the sceptre. She lives. And then she throws the dinner party that ends an empire's second in command.",
